Overlay patch 0013: CMakeLists.txt iOS app target (Spaghettify analog of
reference soh 0004 / 2ship mm 0004) + new ios/Info.plist.in.

Upstream ALREADY carries an embryonic iOS branch, written against a
different LUS fork: it includes a vendored cmake/ios.toolchain.cmake with
PLATFORM hardcoded OS64 (clobbers simulator builds) and bundles
libultraship/ios/{Launch.storyboard,plist.in,...} which DO NOT EXIST in the
Kenix3 LUS at our pin. This patch repoints that skeleton at the proven
reference shape:
- top if(IOS): keep PLATFORM_IOS=1 (Game.cpp's extern-C main guard); drop
  the vendored toolchain include (LUS's ios-toolchain-populate + our
  overlay 0006 own platform selection; -DPLATFORM comes from the command
  line) and the placeholder team/bundle ids.
- app-target branch: our Info.plist.in (added by this patch), shell wiring
  via -DSOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR (SOH_* names kept for harbour-shell uniformity),
  __IOS__ PRIVATE on the game target (LUS's is PRIVATE to itself, reference
  D4), main=SDL_main scoped to src/port/Game.cpp only (SDL2main's UIKit
  shim provides main() -> SDL_main), spaghetti.o2r bundled via
  -DSOH_O2R_PATH. torch's config.yml/yamls/meta self-bundle via upstream's
  existing POST_BUILD copies to $<TARGET_FILE_DIR> (= the .app on iOS).
- deps branch: static ogg/vorbis via -DSOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX (no opus — SoH
  speech-synth only; no SDL2_net — USE_NETWORKING off), SDL2-static +
  SDL2main from LUS's FetchContent, Threads.
Deltas vs 2ship 0004: no PCH prelude (no target_precompile_headers here);
no gamecontrollerdb.txt (upstream never bundles one; LUS warns and
continues).

rev2 (visionOS Phase 01, VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK §1.1): SOH_VISIONOS=1
(cache var from build-visionos.sh / build-vision-sim.sh) gates the vision
deltas INSIDE the same three replacement blocks — zero new vendor anchors:
- Swift @main entry (SohVisionApp.swift) in its OWN flag-clean static lib:
  the Xcode generator ignores COMPILE_LANGUAGE genexes when composing
  OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS, so a .swift source on the game target would inherit
  C warning flags and swiftc hard-errors (reference 0004 trap).
  -Wl,-force_load extracts main from the archive; SDL2main is NOT linked
  on visionOS (genex in the deps branch). ImGui's PUBLIC SDL2::SDL2main
  link in LUS ios.cmake is benign: its main-defining archive member is
  never extracted once @main resolves main (reference-shipped this way).
  SohHostViewController.m + SohImmersive.m ride on the app target;
  frameworks CompositorServices/ARKit/AVFAudio (3D needs all three;
  harmless in Phase 01).
- Info.plist gains @SOH_PLIST_EXTRA@: UIApplicationSceneManifest with
  UIApplicationSupportsMultipleScenes=true, visionOS-only (the SwiftUI
  ImmersiveSpace requires it; top-level placement is silently ignored —
  it must live INSIDE the manifest dict; the key changes UIKit scene
  behavior on iPhone so it stays vision-gated).
Requires the 0038 dispatch analog (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME visionOS -> "iOS"
re-flip) for any of these branches to fire on a visionOS configure.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -105,13 +105,15 @@
 endif()
 
 if(IOS)
-  set(PLATFORM "OS64")
-  include(cmake/ios.toolchain.cmake)
+  # PLATFORM_IOS gates upstream's extern-C main() (src/port/Game.cpp) and
+  # mobile paths. Platform/toolchain selection is owned by libultraship's
+  # ios-toolchain-populate.cmake (overlay 0006 makes PLATFORM overridable:
+  # pass -DPLATFORM=SIMULATORARM64 for simulator builds) — upstream's
+  # vendored cmake/ios.toolchain.cmake hardcoded OS64 and its
+  # libultraship/ios resource dir does not exist in this LUS.
   add_compile_definitions(
     PLATFORM_IOS=1
 )
-  set(CMAKE_XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM "YOUR_TEAM_ID")
-  set(PROJECT_ID "dev.net64.game")
 endif()
 
 ################################################################################
@@ -320,23 +322,121 @@
 list(FILTER ALL_FILES EXCLUDE REGEX "./src/debug/crash_screen_enhancement.c")
 
 if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS")
-  set(IOS_DIR ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/libultraship/ios)
+  add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME} ${ALL_FILES})
 
-  set(STORYBOARD_FILE ${IOS_DIR}/Launch.storyboard)
-  set(IMAGE_FILES ${IOS_DIR}/PoweredBy.png)
-  set(ICON_FILES ${IOS_DIR}/Icon.png)
+  # LUS defines __IOS__ only PRIVATE to itself; Spaghettify TUs (and the
+  # LUS headers they include, plus GameExtractor's mobile paths) need it.
+  # MA_NO_DEVICE_IO: HMAS runs miniaudio with noDevice=MA_TRUE (LUS's
+  # AudioPlayer owns output); without it miniaudio's iOS backend drags
+  # AVFoundation ObjC headers into plain C++ TUs and fails to compile.
+  target_compile_definitions(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE __IOS__ MA_NO_DEVICE_IO)
 
-  list(APPEND ALL_FILES ${STORYBOARD_FILE} ${IMAGE_FILES} ${ICON_FILES})
+  # SDL2main's UIKit shim provides the real main() -> UIApplicationMain ->
+  # SDL_main. Upstream's main() (src/port/Game.cpp, already extern "C"
+  # under PLATFORM_IOS) must therefore BE SDL_main. Scoped to the one file
+  # so no other identifier named `main` can be rewritten. On visionOS the
+  # Swift @main App is the entry instead (SDL2main is NOT linked, see deps
+  # branch); SohHostViewController calls SDL_main once the scene is live.
+  set_source_files_properties(src/port/Game.cpp PROPERTIES
+      COMPILE_DEFINITIONS main=SDL_main)
 
-  add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME} ${ALL_FILES})
-  set_xcode_property(${PROJECT_NAME} PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER ${PROJECT_ID} All)
-  set_target_properties(
-        ${PROJECT_NAME}
-        PROPERTIES
-        MACOSX_BUNDLE TRUE
-        MACOSX_BUNDLE_INFO_PLIST ${IOS_DIR}/plist.in
-        RESOURCE "${IMAGE_FILES};${STORYBOARD_FILE};${ICON_FILES}"
-    )
+  # iOS app shell (touch controls, scene graft, console bridge) lives in
+  # the SpaghettiKart-ios repo, passed as SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR (reference
+  # variable names kept for harbour-shell/script uniformity).
+  if(NOT EXISTS "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/SohIosShell.m")
+      message(FATAL_ERROR "iOS build requires -DSOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR=<dir with SohIosShell.m>")
+  endif()
+  target_sources(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/SohIosShell.m")
+  target_include_directories(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}")
+  target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE "-framework UniformTypeIdentifiers"
+                                                "-framework GameController")
+
+  # Remote console bridge — dev/OTA builds only. SohIosShell.m's #ifndef
+  # fallback pins SOH_REMOTE_CONSOLE to 0, and 0023 gates the "Remote Console"
+  # menu widget on the SAME macro, so when no define reaches this target both
+  # the TCP listener and its toggle compile out. That is exactly what a public
+  # GitHub build wants; dev/OTA builds pass -DSOH_REMOTE_CONSOLE=ON
+  # (build-ios.sh / build-visionos.sh default it ON, public releases run them
+  # with OFF). This MUST sit on ${PROJECT_NAME}: that single target compiles
+  # both SohIosShell.m (the bridge) and src/port/ui/PortMenu.cpp (the toggle),
+  # so one definition brings the pair back together. If a dev build shows no
+  # toggle, the define is not reaching PortMenu.cpp's target.
+  option(SOH_REMOTE_CONSOLE "Compile in the remote console bridge (dev/OTA builds only)" OFF)
+  if(SOH_REMOTE_CONSOLE)
+      target_compile_definitions(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE SOH_REMOTE_CONSOLE=1)
+      message(STATUS "REMOTE CONSOLE COMPILED IN — do not publish this build")
+  else()
+      message(STATUS "remote console compiled out (public-safe)")
+  endif()
+
+  # App icon: ONE asset catalog holds both the iOS AppIcon.appiconset and the
+  # visionOS AppIcon.solidimagestack (layered) — actool compiles whichever
+  # matches the target platform. Registered unconditionally: this branch runs
+  # for visionOS too (0039 flips CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME to "iOS"), and the
+  # ASSETCATALOG_COMPILER_APPICON_NAME + plist CFBundleIconName below point
+  # both platforms' home-screen/App-Library icon at "AppIcon".
+  target_sources(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/Assets.xcassets")
+  set_source_files_properties("${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/Assets.xcassets"
+      PROPERTIES MACOSX_PACKAGE_LOCATION Resources)
+
+  if(SOH_VISIONOS)
+    # SwiftUI app entry in its OWN static lib: the Xcode generator ignores
+    # COMPILE_LANGUAGE genexes when composing OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS, so any
+    # .swift source on the game target inherits its C warning flags and
+    # swiftc hard-errors. Swift's @main emits main; -force_load extracts it
+    # from the archive exactly like SDL2main's shim would have (SDL2main is
+    # NOT linked on visionOS — see the deps branch genex). The SDK swift
+    # -L is needed because the app target has no Swift sources, so Xcode
+    # won't add runtime search paths itself.
+    enable_language(Swift)
+    add_library(sohvisionswift STATIC "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/SohVisionApp.swift")
+    set_target_properties(sohvisionswift PROPERTIES
+        XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_SWIFT_VERSION "5.0"
+        XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_SWIFT_OBJC_BRIDGING_HEADER "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/SohVision-Bridging-Header.h")
+    target_sources(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE
+        "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/SohHostViewController.m"
+        "${SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR}/SohImmersive.m")
+    target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE
+        "-Wl,-force_load,$<TARGET_FILE:sohvisionswift>"
+        "-L$(SDKROOT)/usr/lib/swift"
+        "-framework CompositorServices" "-framework ARKit" "-framework AVFAudio")
+    add_dependencies(${PROJECT_NAME} sohvisionswift)
+  endif()
+
+  # spaghetti.o2r is ROM-independent, produced by the host build
+  # (scripts/extract-mk64-o2r.sh) and bundled as a resource. mk64.o2r is
+  # generated ON DEVICE from the user's ROM by the in-app extractor.
+  set(SOH_O2R_PATH "" CACHE FILEPATH "Path to a host-built spaghetti.o2r to bundle")
+  if(NOT EXISTS "${SOH_O2R_PATH}")
+      message(FATAL_ERROR "iOS build requires -DSOH_O2R_PATH=<host-built spaghetti.o2r>")
+  endif()
+  target_sources(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE "${SOH_O2R_PATH}")
+  set_source_files_properties("${SOH_O2R_PATH}"
+      PROPERTIES MACOSX_PACKAGE_LOCATION Resources)
+
+  set(SOH_IOS_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER "com.harbourmasters.spaghettikart" CACHE STRING "iOS bundle identifier")
+  set(SOH_IOS_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM "" CACHE STRING "Development team for iOS code signing")
+  # visionOS: the SwiftUI entry's ImmersiveSpace (stereo 3D) requires
+  # multiple scenes. The key must sit INSIDE UIApplicationSceneManifest
+  # (top-level placement is silently ignored) and stays visionOS-only
+  # (it changes UIKit scene behavior on iPhone).
+  set(SOH_PLIST_EXTRA "")
+  if(SOH_VISIONOS)
+    set(SOH_PLIST_EXTRA "\n\t<key>UIApplicationSceneManifest</key>\n\t<dict>\n\t\t<key>UIApplicationSupportsMultipleScenes</key>\n\t\t<true/>\n\t</dict>")
+  endif()
+  configure_file(${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/ios/Info.plist.in ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/ios/Info.plist @ONLY)
+  set_target_properties(${PROJECT_NAME} PROPERTIES
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_CLANG_ENABLE_OBJC_ARC YES
+      MACOSX_BUNDLE TRUE
+      MACOSX_BUNDLE_INFO_PLIST "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/ios/Info.plist"
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER "${SOH_IOS_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER}"
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM "${SOH_IOS_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM}"
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_CODE_SIGN_STYLE "Automatic"
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY "1,2"
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_ASSETCATALOG_COMPILER_APPICON_NAME "AppIcon"
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_INSTALL_PATH "$(LOCAL_APPS_DIR)"
+      XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_SKIP_INSTALL "NO"
+  )
 else()
   add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME} ${ALL_FILES})
 endif()
@@ -520,6 +620,45 @@
   target_include_directories(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE
         ${DEVKITPRO}/portlibs/wiiu/include/
     )
+elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS")
+  # SDL2 comes statically from libultraship's FetchContent (SDL2::SDL2-static
+  # + SDL2::SDL2main, linked PUBLIC via ImGui; SDL2main repeated here so the
+  # UIKit main shim is always pulled in — except on visionOS, where the Swift
+  # @main is the entry: the genex drops the explicit link, and ImGui's PUBLIC
+  # SDL2::SDL2main is benign because its main-defining archive member is
+  # never extracted once @main resolves main). Static ogg/vorbis are prebuilt
+  # for iOS and injected by prefix (scripts/build-audio-deps-ios.sh). No opus
+  # (SoH speech-synth only) and no SDL2_net (USE_NETWORKING off).
+  set(THREADS_PREFER_PTHREAD_FLAG ON)
+  find_package(Threads REQUIRED)
+  set(SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX "" CACHE PATH "Prefix containing static ogg/vorbis for iOS")
+  foreach(_l ogg vorbis vorbisenc vorbisfile)
+    if(NOT EXISTS "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/lib/lib${_l}.a")
+      message(FATAL_ERROR "iOS build requires -DSOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX with lib/lib${_l}.a (got '${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}')")
+    endif()
+  endforeach()
+  add_library(Ogg::ogg STATIC IMPORTED)
+  set_target_properties(Ogg::ogg PROPERTIES IMPORTED_LOCATION "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/lib/libogg.a"
+      INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/include")
+  add_library(Vorbis::vorbis STATIC IMPORTED)
+  set_target_properties(Vorbis::vorbis PROPERTIES IMPORTED_LOCATION "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/lib/libvorbis.a"
+      INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/include")
+  add_library(Vorbis::vorbisenc STATIC IMPORTED)
+  set_target_properties(Vorbis::vorbisenc PROPERTIES IMPORTED_LOCATION "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/lib/libvorbisenc.a"
+      INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/include")
+  add_library(Vorbis::vorbisfile STATIC IMPORTED)
+  set_target_properties(Vorbis::vorbisfile PROPERTIES IMPORTED_LOCATION "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/lib/libvorbisfile.a"
+      INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX}/include")
+  set(ADDITIONAL_LIBRARY_DEPENDENCIES
+        SDL2::SDL2-static
+        "$<$<NOT:$<BOOL:${SOH_VISIONOS}>>:SDL2::SDL2main>"
+        "Ogg::ogg"
+        "Vorbis::vorbis"
+        "Vorbis::vorbisenc"
+        "Vorbis::vorbisfile"
+        ${CMAKE_DL_LIBS}
+        Threads::Threads
+    )
 else()
   find_package(Ogg REQUIRED)
   find_package(Vorbis REQUIRED)
